$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 5,5′-Bistrimethylsilyl-2,3′-bithiophene (4). Compound 2
(1.4842 g, 5.26 mmol 1.2 equiv), 3-bromo-5- trimethylsilylthiophene (3)
(1.0312 g, 4.38 mmol 1.0 equiv), K2CO3 (1.5148 g, 10.96 mmol, 2.5 equiv),
and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.1013 g, 87.66 μmol, 0.02 equiv) were added into THF (20
mL) and water (2 mL) under argon. The mixture was stirred for 15 h at 100
°C. The reaction mixture was extracted with chloroform (3 × 35 mL) and
finally dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After the solvent was removed in
vacuo, the residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
with petroleum ether (60-90 °C) as eluent. 4 (1.2255 g, 90%) as a white
solid. Mp: 42-44 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.61 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H),
7.41 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H), 7.26 (d, J = 4 Hz, 1H), 7.17 (d, J = 4 Hz, 1H),
0.35 (s, 9H), 0.34 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 144.15, 141.47,
138.83, 136.87, 134.64, 132.99, 124.98, 124.44, -0.07, -0.12. IR (KBr):
3095, 3057, 2955, 2895 (C-H) cm-1. HRMS (EI+): m/z calcd for
[C14H22S2Si2] 310.0702, found 310.0698.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Characterization of Cyclooctatetrathiophenes with Different
Connection Sequences
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
