$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: II. Experimental for the Suzuki-Miyaura
reaction of lithium triisopropylborates with aryl halides and
pseudohalides. An oven-dried screw cap test tube was charged with
precatalyst 13 (1.0-3.0%) and lithium triisopropylborate (0.375 mmol).
The test tube was evacuated and backfilled with argon (this sequence was
carried out three times). The aryl halide (0.25 mmol) was added via
syringe through the septum (solid aryl halides were added with the
borate), followed by the addition of THF (0.5 mL) and aqueous potassium
phosphate (0.5 M, 1.0 mL). The reaction mixture was subsequently stirred
in a preheated oil bath at 40 °C for 2 h. The tube was taken out of the
oil bath and water (20 mL) and NH4Cl aq. sat. (0.4 mL) were then added.
The mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 20 mL). The combined organic
phases were dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The crude material so obtained was purified via the Biotage
Isolera Four (silica-packed 10 g snap column; EtOAc/hexanes).
2-Methyl-6-(pyridin-4-yl)quinoline (21). Following the general procedure,
a mixture of 4-Bromopyridine hydrochloride (49mg, 0.25 mmol), lithium
triisopropyl 6-(2-methylquinolinyl)borate (253 mg, 0.75 mmol), and 13 (3
mol%) yielded the title compound in 49 mg (89% yield) as a colorless
solid. Mp 102 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 8.70 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H),
8.11 (dd, J = 8.5, 4.5 Hz, 2H), 8.02 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.94 (dd, J =
8.8, 2.1 Hz, 1H), 7.61 (dd, J = 4.7, 1.6 Hz, 2H), 7.34 (d, J = 8.4 Hz,
1H), 2.77 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 160.0, 150.4, 147.9,
147.6, 136.5, 135.2, 129.6, 128.1, 126.5, 125.9, 122.8, 121.8, 25.5.
IR(neat, cm-1): 2361, 1594, 1490, 1413, 1393, 1227. Anal Calcd. for
C15H12N2: C, 81.79; H, 5.49. Found: C, 81.58; H, 5.68. 1H and 13C NMR
spectra included.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General Method for Suzuki-Miyaura Coupling Reactions Using Lithium
Triisopropyl Borates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Oberli, Matthias A.; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(17), 4606-4609

