$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure for Preparation of
Methoxo(5,10,15-tris(5,2'-bithien-2-yl)subporphyrinato)boron(III) (4) To
a mixture of 3 (29.9 mg, 41.2 μmol), 2-thiopheneboronic acid (32.2 mg,
252 μmol), and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.9 mg, 2 mol%) in a Schlenk tube, THF (2.0 mL)
and 2M Na2CO3 (0.5 mL) were added. The resulting solution was
deoxygenated via three freeze-pump-thaw cycles, and then refluxed for 24
h. The resulting mixture was poured into a saturated solution of ammonium
chloride and extracted with CHCl3. The organic layer was washed with
brine and dried over Na2SO4. After the solvent was evaporated, the
residue was separated through a GPC column with CHCl3 as an eluent. Pure
4 was obtained by recrystallization from CH2Cl2/MeOH as a purple solid
(28.9 mg, 89%).
Methoxo(5,10,15-tris(5,2'-bithien-2-yl)subporphyrinato)boron(III) (4),
Yield (28.9 mg, 89%). 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.37 (s, 6H, β), 7.83 (d,
J = 3.7 Hz, 3H, Ha), 7.50 (d, J = 3.7 Hz, 3H, Hb), 7.39 (dd, J = 3.7 and
1.2 Hz, 3H, Hc), 7.32 (dd, J = 5.0 and 1.2 Hz, 3H, He), 7.12 (dd, J = 5.0
and 3.7 Hz, 3H, Hd), and 0.96 (s, 3H, axial-methoxy); 11B NMR (193 MHz,
CDCl3) δ -14.6 (s, 1B); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 141.1, 140.4, 137.7,
137.2, 131.7, 128.2, 125.2, 125.1, 124.3, 122.7, 114.2, and 47.2; HR-ESI
TOF-MS m/z = 734.0148 (calcd for C39H21B1N3S6 = 734.0154 [M - OMe]+);
UV-vis (in CH2Cl2) λ [nm](ε [M-1 cm-1]) 420(130000) and 557(36000).
Fluorescence (in CH2Cl2, λex = 420 nm); λmax [nm] = 680, ΦF = 0.33.
