$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure A for Table 2 (Table
2, Entry 1, as an Example) and Compound 8. A mixture of
3,5-dichloropyridazine (149 mg, 1.00 mmol), phenylboronic acid (122 mg,
1.00 mmol), palladium(II) acetate (11.23 mg, 0.05 mmol),
1,1'-bis-(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene (27.7 mg, 0.05 mmol), and cesium
carbonate (815 mg, 2.50 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane (4.0 mL) and water (1.0 mL)
was degassed for 10 min with N2 and sealed in a microwave vial. The
reaction was heated at 70 &#x00B0;C for 20 h. The reaction was cooled to
room temperature, diluted with ethyl acetate (20 mL), filtered through
Celite, and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (0-100% EtOAc/hexanes) and afforded the product
5-chloro-3-phenylpyridazine (4a) Compound 4m. Representative procedure A
in 89% yield (230 mg) as an amorphous solid. The ratio of the crude
products is 94:1:5 (C3 coupling/C5 coupling/bis coupling): 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) &#x3B4; 8.28 (s, 1H), 7.97 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 7.85 (s, 1H),
7.41 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 7.11 (s, 1H), 6.58 (s, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 2.81
(s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) &#x3B4; 160.0, 156.4, 130.4, 129.1,
126.7, 123.8, 120.9, 120.4, 110.1, 102.4, 33.2, 25.1; HRMS (ESI-Orbitrap)
m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C14H13N3Cl 258.0793, found 258.0791.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, microwave vial used, Suzuki coupling, ratio of the C3
coupling:C5 coupling:bis coupling = 94:1:5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ligand-Dependent Site-Selective Suzuki Cross-Coupling of
3,5-Dichloropyridazines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Dai, Xing; Chen, Yonggang; Garrell, Stephanie; Liu, Hong; Zhang, Li-Kang;
Palani, Anandan; Hughes, Gregory; Nargund, Ravi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(15), 7758-7763

