$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A: Purification by
filtration through a silica gel plug On the bench-top, into a 10 mL screw
vial (46 x 22.5) the Pd catalyst, aryl-halide, MIDA boronate, and Teflon®
stir bar were added to the vial that was then capped. The vial was
briefly degassed with Argon for less than 1 min. The base was then added
followed by 2 wt % TPGS-750-M/H2O via syringe. The vial top was wrapped
using Parafilm® and allowed to stir vigorously at RT for 16-24 h. Upon
completion, 5 mL of 26.5g/g aq. NaCl was added to the vial and the
contents were briefly stirred and then transferred to a separatory funnel
and extracted with EtOAc (3 x 25 mL). The organic phases were collected
and the solvent removed via rotary evaporation @ <100 torr, with the
water bath temperature at or under 40 °C. The crude material was
dissolved in an EtOAc/heptane mixture and transferred to a glass frit
with silica gel while under a vacuum line. The filtrate was collected and
the solvent was removed via rotary evaporation at <100 torr, with the
water bath temperature at or under 40 °C, affording the desired product.
Note: The amount of silica gel and solvent required in the extraction and
filtration steps were NOT optimized. Synthesis of 5-(p-tolyl)pyrimidine
(Scheme 1) The title compound was obtained according to the general
procedure A: (dtbpf)PdCl2 (6.6 mg, 2.0 mol %), 5-bromopyrimidine (79.5
mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv), 4-tolylboronic acid MIDA ester (123.5 mg, 0.5
mmol, 1.0 equiv), Et3N (210 μL, 1.5 mmol, 3.0 equiv), and 2 wt %
TPGS-750-M/H2O (1 mL, 0.5 M). The crude product was purified by silica
gel filtration (eluent: 20% EtOAc/heptane (50 mL), 1.6 g of silica gel,
~1 inch diameter glass frit). The desired compound as a tan powder (76
mg, 89% yield). Synthesis of 5-(6-methoxypyridin-3-yl)pyrimidine (Scheme
2) The title compound was obtained according to the general procedure A:
(dtbpf)PdCl2 (6.6 mg, 2.0 mol %), 5-bromopyrimidine (79.5 mg, 0.5 mmol,
1.0 equiv), 6-methoxypyridin-3-yl boronic acid MIDA ester (132 mg, 0.5
mmol, 1.0 equiv), Et3N (210 μL, 1.5 mmol, 3.0 equiv), and 2 wt %
TPGS-750-M/H2O (1 mL, 0.5 M). The crude product was purified by silica
gel filtration (eluent: 20% EtOAc/heptane w/ 1% Et3N (150 mL), 1.6 g of
silica gel, ~1 inch diameter glass frit). The desired compound as an
off-white powder (83 mg, 89% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, ref:
chloroform): δ 9.19 (s, 1H), 8.90 (s, 2H), 8.38 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 7.77
(dd, J = 2.5, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 6.88 (d, J = 9.3 Hz, 1H), 3.98 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, Suzuki-Miyaura coupling, micellar catalysis
used, alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
