2-(5-(hydroxymethyl)-3-methylisoxazol-4-yl)-4,5-dimethylthiophene-3-carboxylate
(6): To a 500 mL round bottom flask containing Pd2(dba)3 (1.13 g, 1.234
mmol), anhydrous K3PO4 (26.5 g, 125 mmol), and
dicyclohexyl(2',6'-dimethoxybiphenyl-2-yl)phosphine (1.00 g, 2.436 mmol)
under a constant atmosphere of N2 (g) was sequentially added a solution
of
(3-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)isoxazol-5-yl)methyl
acetate (5) (29.8 g, 106 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane (65 mL) and a solution of
methyl 2-bromo-4,5-dimethylthiophene-3-carboxylate (4) (15.07 g, 60.5
mmol) in n-BuOH (250 mL). The resultant suspension was evacuated and
flushed with N2 (g) (3x) and the reaction mixture was subsequently heated
to 100 °C. After 1 h, the reaction mixture was cooled to ambient
temperatures and filtered through a plug of Celite. The filter cake was
washed with MTBE (3 x 100 mL) and the resultant filtrate was sequentially
washed with 1 N HCl (until the pH of the aqueous layer was ~1), saturated
NaHCO3 (150 mL), brine (50 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated to
give a brown oil. To a solution of the Suzuki coupled product in MeOH
(200 mL) was introduced NaOMe (2.2 g, 40.7 mmol). After stirring for ~1.5
h, LC-MS analysis indicated complete conversion to free alcohol. The
reaction mixture was carefully concentrated in vacuo (~75% of MeOH was
removed) and diluted with MTBE. The organic layer was sequentially washed
with 1 N HCl, sat. NaHCO3, brine, dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated to
give a dark brown oil. The oil was purified on Biotage system (gradient
Elution 5% EtOAc : 95% Hexane to 40% EtOAc : 60% Hexanes, then isocratic
40% EtOAc : 60% Hexanes). Methyl 2-
(5-(hydroxymethyl)-3-methylisoxazol-4-yl)-4,5-dimethylthiophene-3-carboxylate
(6) (14.94 g, 53.1 mmol, 88% Yield) as a colorless yellow oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
